Two changes in the program that emulates the robot's own interface. (1) init() promised a value and ended without returning one. Older compilers let that pass; with the current one the program crashed at start ('stack smashing detected') and no robot state was published at all. (2) OpenCV 4 (ROS Noetic) dropped the old name CV_LOAD_IMAGE_UNCHANGED; cv::IMREAD_UNCHANGED is the same value.

